Here's a template for calculating the offset of an element in an array:

```javascript
// Define the array
const array = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];

// Define the index of the element you want to find the offset of
const index = 2;

// Calculate the offset using the formula: offset = index - array.length
const offset = index - array.length;

console.log(offset); // Output: 1
```

Alternatively, you can use the `indexOf()` method:

```javascript
const array = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const index = array.indexOf(3);

console.log(index); // Output: 2
```

Or, you can use the `indexOf()` method with the `Math.abs()` function to get the absolute offset:

```javascript
const array = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const index = Math.abs(array.indexOf(3));

console.log(index); // Output: 2
```

